  "solution": "<p>E equals 2. A exceeds 2 since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>; B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>; C exceeds 2 since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>For D, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, so its reciprocal exceeds 2. Thus E is strictly smallest. <strong>Answer E.</strong></p>",
